  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-01-04T02:30:46.671Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The item system seems to only allow purchased items to be spawned at this time, but it would be very useful for avatar makers to be able to upload and spawn their own props and other elements as avatar-independent items. \n\nAs it is, these items must be baked into avatars, worsening their performance ranking in most cases due to additional meshes, materials and tris from the added props. Also, the nature of this means you can't use props across multiple avatars without a ton of repeated work per-avatar, which could be easily resolved with user-defined spawnable items.\n\nThis could also help with the marketplace, allowing people to make and sell high-quality props and items for others to use, without the need to learn how to make them via unity and blender.",
